/-!
The closedness of the realization sets in the tuple from Lemma 3 at a fixed point (§2.1–2.2;
step 9).

`RealizationSetsZariskiClosed` asks, at a point x and for a divisor D, that the coefficient
matrices c of the tuples (Σ_k c_ik b_k)_i realizing a rational profile α ≥ 0 form a Zariski
closed set. Here it is derived from Lemma 3 of the manuscript at the fixed point x, stated as
`IdealThresholdZariskiClosed`: for every family of elements g_j(c) of the local ring at x that
depend polynomially on parameters c, the set of parameters for which some prime divisor e of a
smooth birational test model, with centre containing x and positive log discrepancy, has
ord_e(g_j(c)) ≥ M A(e) for all nonzero g_j(c) is Zariski closed. That condition says
lct_x(𝔞_c) ≤ 1/M for the ideal 𝔞_c generated by the g_j(c), so the statement is the
semicontinuity of the threshold of a polynomial family of ideals, restricted to x; it does not
depend on D.

The reduction is the algebra of §2.2 (`FlagValuationConditions`) in tuple form:
* along a prime divisor e whose centre contains x, the coefficient of the pullback of the zero
  divisor of a section is the order of its local coefficient at x
  (`cartierPullback_zeroDivisor_coefficient_eq_ord`), because a local equation at x is one at
  every generization of x;
* the local coefficient is linear, so the local coefficients of the tuple are linear forms in c;
* with α_i e_i = M ≥ 2 for natural numbers e_i (`exists_common_exponents`), the bounds
  ord_e(s_i) ≥ α_i A(e) for α_i > 0 are the bounds ord_e(s_i^{e_i}) ≥ M A(e) for the generators
  s_i^{e_i}, which are polynomial in c; the bounds with α_i = 0 always hold, the zero divisors
  being effective.

Hence F1 follows from the sum form of the Kawamata–Viehweg statement, Lemma 3 at the closed
points of the smooth variety with zero boundary, the closedness of the realization sets in the
point, Lemma 3 in its degeneration form and the local statement with the fixed part
(`mixedFujitaFreeness_of_kawamataViehwegSum_of_lemmaThree_of_thresholdBaseModel`).
-/

@[expose] public section

